# regenerate: d2 agent-isolation.d2 agent-isolation.svg
# Hermes agent hard isolation — ADR-0011.
# Each agent = own Discord bot identity + own token + own MCP tool scope.
# Dashed/grey = not built yet, illustrates the pattern for a future agent.

keyvault: Azure Key Vault\nkv-hl-568f36f0\none secret per agent\nhermes-agent-<name>-discord-bot-token {shape: rectangle}
eso: External Secrets Operator\nClusterSecretStore azure-keyvault {shape: rectangle}
hindsight: Hindsight\nmemory service\n(NAS, docker-compose)\nshared long-term memory store {shape: rectangle; style.fill: "#e6f2ff"}

pod: hermes-agent pod (one container, one HERMES_HOME) {
  shape: rectangle
  style.stroke-width: 2

  default: default profile {
    shape: rectangle
    style.fill: "#eeeeee"
    desc: No Discord token.\nNo platform enabled.\nContainer-internal:\ndashboard / admin only. {shape: text}
  }

  delamain: delamain profile {
    shape: rectangle
    bot: own Discord bot\n(concierge identity) {shape: rectangle}
    tools: mcp_servers:\njellyfin, tavily {shape: rectangle}
    mem: memory: provider hindsight {shape: rectangle; style.fill: "#e6f2ff"}
    job: Role: finds food + picks\nsomething to watch {shape: text}
    bot -> tools
  }

  cyberpunk: gm_cyberpunk_rpg profile {
    shape: rectangle
    bot: own Discord bot\n(GM identity) {shape: rectangle}
    tools: mcp_servers:\n(none — narrative only) {shape: rectangle}
    mem: memory: provider hindsight {shape: rectangle; style.fill: "#e6f2ff"}
    job: Role: cyberpunk RPG\ngame master {shape: text}
    bot -> tools
  }

  researcher: gm_researcher profile {
    shape: rectangle
    bot: own Discord bot\n(researcher identity) {shape: rectangle}
    tools: mcp_servers:\n(none yet — web search candidate) {shape: rectangle}
    mem: memory: provider hindsight {shape: rectangle; style.fill: "#e6f2ff"}
    job: Role: sourced,\nrigorous Q&A {shape: text}
    bot -> tools
  }

  calendar: calendar-agent profile\n(not built — illustrates the pattern) {
    shape: rectangle
    style.stroke-dash: 3
    style.opacity: 0.6
    bot: own Discord bot {shape: rectangle; style.stroke-dash: 3; style.opacity: 0.6}
    tools: mcp_servers:\ngoogle-calendar (ONLY here —\nno other profile has this scope) {shape: rectangle; style.stroke-dash: 3; style.opacity: 0.6}
    job: Role: the one agent\nallowed to read/write\nyour calendar {shape: text}
    bot -> tools
  }
}

discord: Discord\n(4 separate bot applications\nprivileged intents enabled\nper application, manual step) {shape: rectangle}

keyvault -> eso: ClusterSecretStore
eso -> pod.delamain.bot: ExternalSecret ->\nfile at /opt/data/profiles/delamain/.env
eso -> pod.cyberpunk.bot: file at\n.../gm_cyberpunk_rpg/.env
eso -> pod.researcher.bot: file at\n.../gm_researcher/.env
eso -> pod.calendar.bot: file at\n.../calendar-agent/.env {style.stroke-dash: 3; style.opacity: 0.6}

pod.delamain.mem -> hindsight: bank_id\nhermes-delamain
pod.cyberpunk.mem -> hindsight: bank_id\nhermes-gm_cyberpunk_rpg
pod.researcher.mem -> hindsight: bank_id\nhermes-gm_researcher

pod.delamain.bot -> discord: connects as\nits own bot user
pod.cyberpunk.bot -> discord
pod.researcher.bot -> discord
pod.calendar.bot -> discord {style.stroke-dash: 3; style.opacity: 0.6}

legend: |md
  **Separation of concerns, enforced architecturally, not by policy:**
  a profile's credentials and MCP tools are resolved from its own scope
  and never unioned into a shared environment (Hermes' own guarantee).
  gm_cyberpunk_rpg can never reach the calendar tool because it's not
  listed in gm_cyberpunk_rpg's config — not because something blocks it.

  Adding a new agent = new Discord bot app (manual) + new Key Vault
  secret + new ExternalSecret + new profile config/SOUL + own gateway
  process (`hermes profile use <name> && hermes gateway start`).

  Dashed = not built yet, shown to illustrate the pattern.

  **Memory is the one shared backend**: all three live agents point at the
  same Hindsight service (NAS, docker-compose), but each uses its own
  `bank_id` (`hermes-<profile>`) — recall never crosses banks, so this
  doesn't violate the isolation model above.
| {shape: text}
